As per Section 2(6) of the CGST Act, 2017, “aggregate turnover” is defined as the aggregate value of all:
*   Taxable supplies (excluding the value of inward supplies on which tax is payable by a person on a reverse charge basis);
*   Exempt supplies;
*   Exports of goods or services or both; and
*   Inter-State supplies of persons having the same Permanent Account Number (PAN).

This aggregate value is to be computed on an all-India basis and excludes Central tax, State tax, Union territory tax, Integrated tax, and Cess (p. 68, p. 194).
